            <ArticleTitle>Use of lipid-modulating drugs in complicated course of coronary heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>438-46</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the results of the study of lipid-modulating drugs (pravastatin, atorvastatin, simvastatin, and fibrate gemfibrozil) in complicated coronary heart disease (acute coronary syndrome without ST elevation, chronic heart failure. In acute coronary syndrome statins produced a positive effect on some studied parameters, while in heart failure only the safety of short-term therapy with statins was demonstrated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
